<Base title="About StagePath" description="Why StagePath publishes deep, public, project-driven learning roadmaps.">
  <article class="about"><span class="eyebrow">About StagePath</span><h1 class="display-title">Learning needs structure,<br /><span>not another feed.</span></h1><p class="intro">StagePath is a public, open-source collection of detailed career roadmaps. It helps learners understand what belongs inside a topic, what order makes sense, and what they can build to prove the skill.</p><section><h2>What it does</h2><p>Every roadmap moves from career stages to major topics, detailed subtopics, learning outcomes, resources, and complete project briefs. The goal is to replace vague advice with a usable map.</p></section><section><h2>What it deliberately does not do</h2><p>StagePath has no accounts, login, personal dashboard, saved progress, certificates, or social feed. It does not pretend that checking boxes creates competence. Learners can use the public maps with any notes or task system they already prefer.</p></section><section><h2>Project-driven by default</h2><p>A project should include a clear problem, scenario, data or working material, requirements, milestones, deliverables, and review criteria. “Build something with React” or “make a dashboard” is not a sufficient brief.</p></section><section><h2>Built to grow beyond one field</h2><p>The first collection spans software development, cybersecurity, UX design, and data. The same content model can support product, business, cloud, creative, and other career families without changing the platform identity.</p></section></article>

</Base>
<style>.about{max-width:850px}.about .display-title{font-size:clamp(44px,6vw,68px)}.about .display-title span{color:var(--green)}.intro{margin:25px 0 55px;color:var(--muted);font-size:19px;line-height:1.7}.about section{display:grid;grid-template-columns:240px 1fr;gap:45px;padding:32px 0;border-top:1px solid var(--line)}.about h2{margin:0;font-size:20px;letter-spacing:-.03em}.about section p{margin:0;color:var(--muted);font-size:14px}@media(max-width:650px){.about section{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:8px}}</style>
